{
  "id": "m24l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "functools: reduce y caché",
    "en": "functools: reduce and caching"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Combinar y recordar"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`reduce(funcion, iterable)` combina los elementos de dos en dos hasta dejar un único resultado (p. ej. el producto de una lista)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from functools import reduce",
          "print(reduce(lambda a, b: a * b, [1, 2, 3, 4]))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "24"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`@lru_cache` **memoiza**: guarda los resultados de una función para no recalcularlos. Acelera muchísimo la recursión, como en Fibonacci."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from functools import lru_cache",
          "",
          "@lru_cache",
          "def fib(n):",
          "    return n if n < 2 else fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)",
          "",
          "print(fib(10))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "55"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "lru_cache solo sirve si la función es 'pura' (mismos argumentos -> mismo resultado, sin efectos colaterales)."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Combine and remember"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`reduce(function, iterable)` combines elements two at a time until a single result remains (e.g. the product of a list)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from functools import reduce",
          "print(reduce(lambda a, b: a * b, [1, 2, 3, 4]))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "24"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`@lru_cache` **memoizes**: it stores a function's results so they aren't recomputed. It hugely speeds up recursion, like Fibonacci."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "from functools import lru_cache",
          "",
          "@lru_cache",
          "def fib(n):",
          "    return n if n < 2 else fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)",
          "",
          "print(fib(10))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "55"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "lru_cache only works if the function is 'pure' (same arguments -> same result, no side effects)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m24l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `producto(numeros)` que devuelva el producto de todos los números de la lista (usa functools.reduce).",
        "en": "Define `producto(numeros)` returning the product of all numbers in the list (use functools.reduce)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "from functools import reduce",
        "",
        "def producto(numeros):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "from functools import reduce",
        "",
        "def producto(numeros):",
        "    return reduce(lambda a, b: a * b, numeros)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "reduce con lambda a, b: a * b."
        ],
        "en": [
          "reduce with lambda a, b: a * b."
        ]
      },
